      "## Social conditions at the beginning of the twentieth century",
      "Industrialization, urbanization, immigration, expanding public education, and rapidly changing work roles created new needs. Young people and adults were expected to make occupational choices in an increasingly complex labor market. Schools were also asked to help students prepare for work, citizenship, and adult life.",
