      "## Licensure and public protection",
      "State licensure developed to regulate who may use protected professional titles or perform regulated counseling activities. Licensure laws define requirements and establish disciplinary authority.",
      "The growth of licensure strengthened public recognition, but it also produced variation in:",
      "- License titles\n- Educational requirements\n- Required examinations\n- Supervised experience\n- Scope language\n- Renewal and continuing-education requirements",
      "This variation remains important for portability and interstate practice.",
      "## CACREP and preparation standards",
      "The Council for Accreditation of Counseling and Related Educational Programs (CACREP) dates to 1981. CACREP evaluates graduate counseling programs against professional standards.",
      "Accreditation contributed to professionalization by supporting:",
      "- Greater consistency in counselor preparation\n- Public identification of programs meeting professional standards\n- Program self-evaluation and external peer review\n- A more unified counseling curriculum and identity",
      "CACREP accredits **programs**, not individual counselors.",
      "## NBCC, the NCC, and the NCE",
      "The National Board for Certified Counselors (NBCC) was established in 1982 as an independent certification organization. The National Certified Counselor (NCC) became a national professional certification.",
