      "## Direct and indirect client care",
      "### Direct client care",
      "The counselor interacts with the client or group to provide a service such as:",
      "- Intake and assessment\n- Individual, group, couples, or family counseling within competence\n- Crisis assessment and intervention\n- Treatment or service planning\n- Career and educational counseling\n- Psychoeducation\n- Rehabilitation counseling\n- Progress monitoring and termination planning",
      "### Indirect client care",
      "The counselor supports client welfare through activities such as:",
      "- Consultation\n- Care coordination\n- Referral and follow-up\n- Collaboration with other professionals\n- Documentation and record management\n- Program planning and evaluation\n- Supervision, when qualified and assigned\n- Advocacy\n- Continuing education and professional development",
      "Indirect care is not `extra` work unrelated to counseling. It can be essential to continuity, ethics, quality, and access.",
      "## Roles by setting",
      "## School counseling as a developmental program",
      "Modern school counseling is not merely reactive scheduling or discipline. Comprehensive programs support academic, career, and social/emotional development through:",
      "- Instruction\n- Appraisal and advisement\n- Short-term individual and group counseling\n- Consultation with families and staff\n- Referral\n- Data-informed program planning\n- Leadership and advocacy",
      "The American School Counselor Association states that school counselors are not disciplinarians. A school counselor can participate in support planning related to behavior while avoiding the role of administering punishment.",
      "## Rehabilitation counseling",
      "Rehabilitation counselors support people with disabilities in achieving psychological, social, vocational, and independent-living goals. The work may include:",
      "- Adjustment to disability\n- Strengths and functional assessment\n- Career and employment planning\n- Accommodation and accessibility\n- Coordination with medical, vocational, educational, and community systems\n- Advocacy against environmental barriers",
      "The focus is not `fixing` the person. It includes participation, choice, access, and person–environment fit.",
      "## Clinical mental health counseling",
      "Clinical mental health counselors may provide assessment, diagnosis, treatment planning, counseling, crisis intervention, and care coordination when authorized and competent.",
      "Two errors should be avoided:",
      "- Assuming all counselors in all settings have identical diagnostic authority\n- Assuming the profession's wellness orientation excludes treatment of mental disorders",
      "Jurisdiction, license level, setting, training, and payer requirements can affect the role.",
      "## Career counseling",
      "Career counseling may address more than occupational selection. It can include:",
      "- Identity and meaning\n- Work–life roles\n- Barriers and discrimination\n- Career transitions\n- Retirement\n- Unemployment and underemployment\n- Disability and accommodation\n- Labor-market information\n- Decision-making difficulty",
      "## Role conflict and multiple stakeholders",
      "In schools, corrections, employee-assistance programs, hospitals, and organizations, multiple parties may have interests in the service.",
      "The counselor should clarify:",
      "- Who the client is\n- The purpose of the service\n- The counselor's role\n- Limits of confidentiality\n- What information may be shared and with whom\n- How records and reports will be used",
